<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuri Igorevich of Ryazan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">?–<a href="/years/1237">1237</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuri Igorevich was Prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a> when Batu's Mongol army invaded north-eastern Rus' in the winter of 1237. Having refused the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>' demand for a tenth of everything, he sought help from Vladimir in vain, and he was killed with his family when Ryazan fell after a short siege in December 1237. His death is told in the Tale of the Destruction of Ryazan by Batu.</p></div>
